From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bastiaan van der Plaat <bastiaan.v.d.plaat@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 07:54:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Size the collision map for each map

The arrays of the collision map are allocated as big as the map needs,
with room for the box hull, instead of 5.5 MiB of static arrays for the
biggest map, and its lumps are read one at a time instead of the whole
file. The visibility and entities, which are seldom read, go to the far
heap. The map checksum is only compared with the local server, which
loaded the same file, so it is always 0.
---
 qcommon/cmodel.c | 219 +++++++++++++++++++++++++----------------------
 1 file changed, 116 insertions(+), 103 deletions(-)

diff --git a/qcommon/cmodel.c b/qcommon/cmodel.c
